  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kiribati has regularly fulfilled its reporting obligations under Articles 19 and 22 of the ILO Constitution. The Kiribati tripartite delegation has also attended ILC in the last three years.
The ILO continues to provide technical assistance to implement ratified conventions and address comments of ILO supervisory bodies, including in relation to fundamental conventions and the MLC. ILO is also supporting the Government to finalize the review of key sets of labour regulations as recommended by ILO supervisory bodies.</narrative>
  </description>
